WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.051 --> 00:00:04.080
- [Carolyn] For as long as I knew Eugene,

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.260
he had his sight set on space.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:11.460
All these years later I can't
believe he's still up there.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:12.960
My man on the moon.

00:00:15.665 --> 00:00:18.582
(slow piano music)

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:29.230
Eugene and I were married 46 years.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:31.130
I first met Eugene when he

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.880
was studying geology at Princeton.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:37.240
He would tell me about all
the secrets the Earth held.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:41.780
And of course his favorite,
those impact craters.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:46.130
Soon enough he got me to fall
in love with those rocks, too.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:49.677
After the kids had grown
and were out of the house,

00:00:49.677 --> 00:00:52.610
I was looking for something to do

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:55.510
and Gene suggested maybe I would like

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:58.180
to see things through the telescope.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.603
We spent our days holed
up in Lowell Observatory.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:05.890
- [Man] I believe that this nation.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.700
- When Kennedy announced
that they were going

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.650
to send a man to the moon,
Gene was terribly excited.

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:16.930
Gene wanted to go to the
moon more than anything else.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.700
Then he got the medical test.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.680
Addison's Disease.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:24.330
His immune system wasn't protecting him

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:25.820
the way it needed to.

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:28.490
They couldn't risk him leaving Earth.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:33.433
He felt like his goal
had suddenly disappeared.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:37.540
At the same time he was not a quitter.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:39.920
He set up his own mock lunar site

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.870
and trained Neil Armstrong and the rest

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.117
of the boys before they took off.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.070
Our focus changed over the years

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:55.710
from looking up at the
moon and looking at the sky

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:59.150
to how the Earth was formed.

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:02.540
We packed up and criss-crossed Australia

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:05.263
looking for signs of impact craters.

00:02:09.285 --> 00:02:10.800
On the day of the accident,

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.040
we were just looking off in the distance,

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.480
talking about how much fun we were having.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.320
And then suddenly there appeared

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.423
a Land Rover in front of us.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.330
There was no time to think.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.490
The two vehicles collided.

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:27.533
And Gene died.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.060
I had a call while I was in the hospital.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.030
He said they're about to send
a mission up to the moon.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:41.430
I wonder if you would like to
put Gene's ashes on the moon,

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:44.603
and so I said I think
that would be wonderful.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:50.010
The whole family was there
to wave Gene goodbye.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.520
After the mission was completed,

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:57.010
it ran out of fuel and
it crashed into the moon.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.373
And that's where Gene's ashes are now.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:03.430
Suddenly the man who spent his whole life

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:07.163
studying craters had made his own impact.

00:03:09.899 --> 00:03:13.370
I miss him always, but to this day

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.984
I can look up at the moon and imagine him

00:03:15.984 --> 00:03:19.770
there with his rocks looking down at me.

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:23.653
He still lights up every
single one of my night skies.

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:31.834
(pinging)

